{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>My vows</b> — the heh at its beginning is superfluous." "<b>And the word na</b> — it is here like every na in Scripture, and it enters the mem [preposition] together with לכל עמו (to all His people), like מימין לבית (from the right side of the house)."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 116, :notes {1 "The cryptographic reference to לכל עמו is preserved as Ibn Ezra gives it; the analogy to מימין לבית is likewise opaque and left untranslated literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:39:51.437328450Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}